{"by_variant":{"minimalsanitized":[{"id":"CA1","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[23],"code":"address public governance;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Governance variable declaration. Not a prerequisite - governance is unused in the vulnerable function."},{"id":"CA2","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[24],"code":"mapping(address => address) public strategies;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Strategy mapping. Not directly vulnerable."},{"id":"CA3","type":"INITIALIZATION","lines":[26,27,28],"code":"constructor() {\n    governance = msg.sender;\n}\n","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Sets governance. Correctly implemented."},{"id":"CA4","type":"INPUT_VAL","lines":[38],"code":"require(_targets.length == _data.length, \"Length mismatch\");","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Array length validation. Correctly checks alignment."},{"id":"CA5","type":"CTRL_FLOW","lines":[40],"code":"for (uint256 i = 0; i < _targets.length; i++) {","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Loop over targets array. This is an amplifier, not a prerequisite - a single unchecked call is already sufficient to exploit."},{"id":"CA6","type":"EXT_CALL","lines":[41,42],"code":"(bool success, ) = _targets[i].call(_data[i]);\nrequire(success, \"Call failed\");\n","security_function":"ROOT_CAUSE","rationale":"ROOT_CAUSE - Arbitrary external call with attacker-controlled target and data. No access control check - anyone can call this function and execute arbitrary contract calls. Attacker can drain funds by calling token.transfer() or approve()."},{"id":"CA7","type":"ACCESS_CTRL","lines":[52,53,54,55],"code":"function setStrategy(address jar, address strategy) external {\n    require(msg.sender == governance, \"Not governance\");\n    strategies[jar] = strategy;\n}\n","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"setStrategy has correct access control. Shows that governance check exists but was not applied to swapExactJarForJar."},{"id":"CA8","type":"DECLARATION","lines":[59,60],